 "rule": "Early skip of the BFS local optimizations of arm J5. A skipped or stopped fit is a rejected fit (the voxel becomes or stays a refit voxel; a skipped neighbour fit holds its start, a skipped revisit keeps the old end). Every check is one counted evaluation. S(t, scope): before the fit, check the start; skip if its hit ratio is under t times the best. C(t, scope): after 20 evaluations, check the running best; stop if under t times the best. D(d): skip a revisit whose start lies within d degrees of a start already rejected at that voxel since its last reset (no evaluation). t in {0.3, 0.4, 0.5, 0.6}; scope revisits, neighbour fits or both; d in {0.1, 0.25, 0.5}: 27 rules.",
 "selection": "A rule is admissible if on each of the five samples (a) wrong skips are at most 0.1% of that sample's fits and (b) at most 2 final answers before the pass change. Among admissible rules take the largest sum over the five samples of the net saving as a share of J5 (saved evaluations of skipped fits that J5 rejected, minus every check; wrong skips earn nothing). Ties: fewer wrong skips in all, then D before S before C, then the smaller t or d.",
